# Testing Development Guide

This guide provides a comprehensive overview of the testing strategy, tools, and procedures used in this project.

## Guiding Principles

-   **Unit Tests**: Test behavior, not implementation. Keep tests small, isolated, and mock external dependencies. Cover error and edge cases.
-   **Integration Tests**: Test realistic user scenarios with minimal mocking, focusing on API contracts and database interactions.
-   **E2E Tests**: Focus on critical user paths. Use `data-testid` attributes for selectors. Implement proper waits and keep tests independent.

## Quick Commands

### Unit & Integration Tests (Jest)

```bash
# Run all unit tests with coverage
npm run test:unit

# Run unit tests in watch mode
npm run test:unit:watch

# Run tests related to specific files
npm run test:unit:subset <file1> <file2>

# Run tests with coverage for a subset of files
npm run test:unit:coverage:subset <file1> <file2>
```

### End-to-End Tests (Playwright)

The E2E scripts automatically handle killing processes on the test port and checking server logs for errors after the run.

```bash
# Run all E2E tests
npm run test:e2e

# Run only authentication-related tests
npm run test:e2e:auth-only

# Run only tests for public (unauthenticated) pages
npm run test:e2e:public-only

# Run only tests for authenticated pages
npm run test:e2e:authenticated-only

# Run Playwright in debug mode
npx playwright test --debug

# View the last HTML test report
npm run test:e2e:report

# Update visual regression snapshots
npm run test:e2e:update-snapshots
```

### Combined & CI

```bash
# Run the primary test suite (unit tests)
npm test

# Run the full CI suite (unit + E2E)
npm run test:ci
```

